  "body": "<style>#fig text.label{font-size:17px}@media (max-width:600px){#fig text.label{font-size:27px}}</style><header class=\"head\"><p class=\"tag\">[diagram, made by Mimir, simplified]</p><h1>The envelope of a Gram-negative bacterium</h1><p class=\"intro\">A Gram-negative bacterium such as E. coli is wrapped in layers. Click through to build its envelope from the inside out.</p></header><div class=\"board\" style=\"--sticky-fig: 9rem\"><figure><svg id=\"fig\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 200\" role=\"img\"><title>Envelope of a Gram-negative bacterium</title><desc>A rod-shaped cell drawn as nested capsule outlines, built from the inside out. Cytoplasm is innermost. Around it is the inner membrane. Outside that is the periplasm, holding the thin cell wall. The outer membrane is outermost, with a fringe of lipopolysaccharide on its outer face. Four labels at the right, Outer membrane, Cell wall, Inner membrane and Cytoplasm, each with a leader line to its layer.</desc><rect class=\"ghost\" x=\"10.0\" y=\"69.5\" width=\"340.0\" height=\"85.0\" rx=\"42.5\" /><g data-step=\"3\"><rect class=\"wash\" x=\"10.0\" y=\"69.5\" width=\"340.0\" height=\"85.0\" rx=\"42.5\" fill=\"var(--wash-ochre)\" stroke=\"none\"/></g><g data-step=\"1\"><rect class=\"wash\" x=\"25.0\" y=\"84.5\" width=\"310.0\" height=\"55.0\" rx=\"27.5\" fill=\"var(--wash-sky)\" stroke=\"none\"/></g><g data-step=\"2\"><rect class=\"ink\" x=\"22.0\" y=\"81.5\" width=\"316.0\" height=\"61.0\" rx=\"30.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\" pathLength=\"1\"/><rect class=\"ink\" x=\"25.0\" y=\"84.5\" width=\"310.0\" height=\"55.0\" rx=\"27.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\" pathLength=\"1\"/></g><g data-step=\"3\"><rect class=\"ink\" x=\"17.5\" y=\"77.0\" width=\"325.0\" height=\"70.0\" rx=\"35.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" pathLength=\"1\"/></g><g data-step=\"4\"><rect class=\"ink\" x=\"10.0\" y=\"69.5\" width=\"340.0\" height=\"85.0\" rx=\"42.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\" pathLength=\"1\"/><rect class=\"