, proteins and ribosomes. The DNA lies in a region called the nucleoid, with no membrane around it.</p></div><div class=\"step\" data-step=\"2\"><div class=\"n\">2</div><p><span class=\"runin\">Inner membrane:</span> a phospholipid bilayer around the cytoplasm that controls what enters and leaves it.</p></div><div class=\"step\" data-step=\"3\"><div class=\"n\">3</div><p><span class=\"runin\">Cell wall:</span> outside the inner membrane lies the periplasm, a narrow space that holds a thin layer of peptidoglycan, the cell wall, which keeps the cell's shape.</p></div><div class=\"step\" data-step=\"4\"><div class=\"n\">4</div><p><span class=\"runin\">Outer membrane:</span> a second bilayer whose outer face carries lipopolysaccharide (LPS); porins in it let small molecules through.</p></div><p class=\"caption caption-phone\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Not to scale: the whole envelope is a few tens of nanometres thick, and the cell about 2 µm long.</p></div></div>"
}
